#: ../../source/getting_started/faq.rst:5
msgid ""
"What are the KV cache sizes for popular models? And why is LMCache "
"important?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/getting_started/faq.rst:7
msgid ""
"You can calculate KV cache sizes using our :doc:`KV cache calculator "
"<kv_cache_calculator>`. We also provide a reference table below with KV "
"cache information for some popular models."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/getting_started/faq.rst:9
msgid ""
"As shown in the table, after loading Qwen/Qwen3-32B for example, there is"
" only enough space in the spare GPU RAM to hold 275,760 tokens for KV "
"caches. This supports only 6.73 concurrent users if each prompt is 40,960"
" tokens long. Once this capacity is exceeded, the KV cache must be "
"evicted, and when the same user returns, their request needs to be re-"
"prefilled, which takes significantly longer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/getting_started/faq.rst:11
msgid ""
"**LMCache is designed to extend this virtual memory capacity**, enabling "
"you to store more KV caches and avoid costly re-prefilling operations."
msgstr ""

